    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_46b10468",
      "@type": "OverallIntent",
      "instance_name": "overallintent_instance",
      "label": "the overallintent",
      "description": "meme-id: a_good_asian_driver; hasOverallIntent: Hateful; overall-intent-description: The image juxtaposes a wooden cross with flowers in a grassy area, symbolizing a memorial or grave, with a car in the background and the text 'a good asian driver'. This visual and textual combination is a harmful stereotype that implies Asian drivers are so dangerous or reckless that they must be memorialized after causing fatal accidents. It weaponizes the 'model minority' myth by mocking Asian drivers' perceived driving abilities, which is a form of anti-Asian racism. The meme is hateful as it targets a specific racial group with a derogatory and potentially dangerous stereotype, suggesting that Asian drivers are inherently dangerous and deserving of death or memorialization, which can contribute to prejudice and discrimination against Asian communities.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_c457936b"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
